<statement>
<p>
	Write a function <pf>create_keyboard_struct</pf>.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>none</pf> number — value</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>keyboard</pf> (struct) number — is a structure containing 26 fields (one for each letter); each of the letters contains a struct with three fields</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Note that this function does not display the game board or the keyboard. No plot/figure is involved in this function. The purpose of this function is only to create the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>keyboard</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>structure.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>A template is provided that generates the top two lines of the keyboard. You should create the code to complete the keyboard structure.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
